    "body": "## Motivation\n\nMiniMax M2 tool arguments with nullable schemas lose valid non-null values. For example, `{\"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"]}` converts the model's `42` to JSON `null`, in both ordinary and streaming responses. Pydantic-style `anyOf` schemas and enums containing `null` have the same problem.\n\n## Modifications\n\nOnly treat the parameter's value as a null marker; allowing `null` in its schema no longer bypasses the existing type converters. Preserve the existing `null`/`none`/`nil` aliases.\n\nAdd CPU tests through `FunctionCallParser(\"minimax-m2\")` for nullable scalar/container types, `anyOf`/`oneOf`, enums, explicit nulls, and non-nullable controls. Exercise ordinary parsing and streaming with complete frames, parameter boundaries, and character splits after the atomic tool-start marker.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- New regression suite: **5 tests and 56 subtests pass**. Before the change, 36 non-null nullable cases fail and 20 control subtests pass.\n- Existing function-parser module plus the new suite: **240 tests and 107 subtests pass**; 15 existing DeepSeek tests requiring unavailable Triton-backed tokenizer setup are deselected.\n- Tests execute the actual protocol and parser source on CPU, bypassing only GPU-facing package initializers in the local harness. No model/GPU inference was run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: this fixes argument conversion and makes no inference-performance claim.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Add focused, CPU-registered regression tests.\n- [x] All applicable pre-commit hooks pass on the two changed files.\n- [x] Follow existing parser and test style.\n- [x] Documentation and model accuracy/speed benchmarks are not required for this localized conversion fix.\n\nAI assistance was used for investigation, implementation, and tests; the change received independent review and before/after validation.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36861136420](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36861136420)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36861135854](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36861135854)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36861136302](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36861136302)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
